{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1535430-tc-aegis-much-more-mythological-gods","id":1535430,"title":"[TC Aegis] Much more mythological Gods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aegis"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-10T23:56:12-07:00","id":1535430,"title":"[TC Aegis] Much more mythological Gods?","content":"<b>Would it be game and genere breaking with making Gods in <i>TC Aegis</i> much more mythical, </b>on pars of those in literal mythical medias? Like <b>Blood of Zeus</b>, for example? The Gods - Pantheon now - is somehow reincarnation of real myths gods - and they have so much stats, Gifts, etc. - so listing all their powers is useless. Hermes is really the fastest being and partially psychopomp ( interesting what does he do with the souls he collect then? ), Zeus is really sky god, Poseidon is real god of the seas, etc. <b>Would setting like that really broke the game?</b><br /> <br /> And I mean that PLAYERS <b><i>won't be</i></b> those Gods - only that there are 'Gods' NPCs in the World. Players, at most, can be Champions, demigods, etc. Well, technically, VERY STRONG Olympian ( like 1000 XP or more ) could be seen as God in that setting - but Gods, on genreal, are on another level than PCs. <br /> <br /> And I would still limit Gods to <b>only one active 'incarnation' existing at the same time in the World</b> of this kind setting. So one 'Zeus', one 'Poseidon', one 'Hermes'. So they would need to move really fast, if they want to full fill their 'domain duties'.<br /> <br /> <b><img width=\"1000\" height=\"563\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/E7o1EFM.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/E7o1EFM.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/E7o1EFM.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-11-2024, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T03:46:50-07:00","id":1535433,"title":"","content":"Aegis isn't a supernatural setting, it's a very comic book take on Ancient Astronauts (i.e. no racism or creepiness, just over-the-top Weirdness). The gods might be a distant spiritual presence subtly manipulating events but that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T04:38:29-07:00","id":1535435,"title":"","content":"I think the Olympian gods are real in canon. They\u2019re just extremely powerful Olympians created by the crash of the AEON and the subsequent spill of ambrosia. At least that was the impression I got from the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T05:47:41-07:00","id":1535438,"title":"","content":"They're real in the sense that they're Aegis-era Novas, yes. The premise of TC:Aegis is that a sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from the supernatural; it isn't <i>actually </i>supernatural.<br /> <br /> Note that introducing actual gods to the setting, as opposed to the likes of Apollo from Star Trek's \u201cWho Mourns For Adonis?\u201d, doesn't actually <i>break </i>anything, per se; it's just not in line with the era's premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Elaborated 05-11-2024, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T07:57:34-07:00","id":1535440,"title":"","content":"In the Storyguide chapter there are a lot of references to how to add the gods to the game. It\u2019s not something that was not covered already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T12:57:40-07:00","id":1535457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1535430-tc-aegis-much-more-mythological-gods?p=1535435#post1535435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Olympian gods are real in canon. They\u2019re just extremely powerful Olympians created by the crash of the AEON and the subsequent spill of ambrosia. At least that was the impression I got from the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. But they wouldn't be the mythical Olympian gods. They'd be the source, or individuals naming themselves after mythical gods and later confused with their namesakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T20:30:34-07:00","id":1549514,"title":"","content":"Really glad Aegis finally came out. Other than Adventure!, it\u2019s my favorite Trinity Continuum game so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T03:34:16-07:00","id":1549520,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here read any of Kirby's <b>Eternals</b>? It's very much a superheroes as inspiration for the mythical gods comic book. Ignore the movie version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T03:54:34-07:00","id":1552913,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that a good book on actual Greek religious practices in period would really be useful for anyone setting up campaigns. Knowing how certain things were done. Where important cult centers were. Or the social details of hero cults of living people (a real thing in period). All these things could create drama and motivate action in ways that fit the period. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}